Z||000000||Greg Piet||08-31-99||08:22 AM||||I have been going to the Las Vegas Motor Speedway quite a bit lately, and there is a division called the "mini street stock"<br>These seem to be little pintos, s-10 trucks, etc...  I saw this division, and thought it might be neat to see a little fiero try this on their 3/8 mile oval.  Unfortunately the division is limited to american cars (ok thats covered), and front engine.  With the first rule in affect, it appears that the second rule exclusively puts the fiero out of the running.  Is there any fiero racing going on?
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-31-99||08:52 AM||||Aside from a couple of guys running the old IMSA GTU tube-frame Fieros in SCCA GT-2, I haven't seen anyone racing Fieros except in autocrosses.<p>A lot of people don't know that the Fiero had a pretty distinguished racing record in both IMSA GTU and GTP-Lights.  I can't remember the details now, but I know it was the first American car to win a GTU race.
